d":"2025-12-01T14:49:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/46302724/week-3-nfl-odds-spreads-lines-props-best-bets-sunday-football-games","type":"Story","byline":"Matt Bowen and Seth Walder","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sunday's loss to Cowboys a microcosm of Panthers' issues","description":"Where might Carolina aim its offseason efforts to improve its roster?","published":"2024-12-17T13:34:40.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/43009104/nfl-carolina-panthers-dallas-cowboys-bryce-young","type":"Story","byline":"David Newton","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Improving Panthers D a boost for Evero's head-coach chances?","description":"After a rough start to 2024, the Panthers' defense has shown signs of life lately.","published":"2024-12-06T13:26:02.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/42792909/nfl-carolina-panthers-defensive-coordinator-ejiro-evero-head-coach","type":"Story","byline":"David Newton","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Panthers RB Jonathon Brooks not expected to play vs. Saints","description":"Panthers rookie running back Jonathon Brooks is not expected to play against the Saints despite being listed as questionable, coach Dave Canales said.","published":"2024-11-01T18:21:33.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/42132850/panthers-rb-jonathon-brooks-not-expected-play-vs-saints","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"David Newton","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Panthers' Jonathon Brooks, D.J. Wonnum out at least 4 games","description":"Panthers rookie RB Jonathon Brooks and LB D.J. Wonnum will miss at least the first four games of the season, while receiver Terrace Marshall Jr. was released.","published":"2024-08-27T23:06:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/41012620/sources-panthers-jonathon-brooks-inactive-4-games","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"David Newton","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2024 Carolina Panthers 53-man roster projection","description":"Here's a look at the Panthers' roster, including why the outside linebacker corps could be vulnerable.","published":"2024-07-23T10:02:20.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/insider/story/_/id/40532413/2024-carolina-panthers-53-man-roster-projection-bryce-young-jadeveon-clowney","type":"Story","byline":"David Newton","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Panthers 2024 free agency tracker: Offseason moves, signings","description":"Keep track of all the Panthers free agent moves throughout the 2024 offseason.","published":"2024-03-27T23:23:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/39575204/panthers-2024-free-agency-tracker-offseason-moves-signings","type":"Story","byline":"David Newton","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"D. J. Wonnum","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/D._J._Wonnum","description":"American football player (born 1997)","touched":"2026-11-22T23:50:14Z","intro":"Dennis O. \"D. J.\" Wonnum Jr (born October 31, 1997) is an American professional football defensive end for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He played college football for the South Carolina Gamecocks. Wonnum was selected by the Minnesota Vikings in the fourth round of the 2020 NFL draft.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Wonnum grew up in Stone Mountain, Georgia, and attended Stephenson High School. As a senior, he was named All-Region after recording 38 tackles with 11 tackles for loss and 2.5 sacks. Wonnum initially committed to play college football at Iowa State before de-committing after a coaching change. He subsequently committed to attend Indiana before de-committing a second time and signing to play at South Carolina."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Wonnum played in all of South Carolina's games as a true freshman, recording 32 tackles including 3.5 tackles for loss and 1.5 sacks. Wonnum was named a permanent team captain going into his sophomore year and finished the season with 57 tackles and led the team with 13.0 tackles for loss and 6.0 sacks. He injured his ankle during the Gamecocks' season opener as a junior, and only played in five games. He compiled 11 tackles, 3.5 tackles for loss and two sacks during the injury-shortened season. As a senior, Wonnum recorded 37 tackles with 9.5 tackles for loss and 4.5 sacks with three quarterback hurries, a forced fumble, one blocked kick, and an interception and was named second-team All-Southeastern Conference."},{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"MINNESOTA VIKINGS\nWonnum was selected by the Minnesota Vikings with the 117th overall pick in the fourth round of the 2020 NFL draft.\nIn Week 4 against the Houston Texans, Wonnum recorded his first career sack on Deshaun Watson during the 31–23 win.\nIn Week 8 against the Green Bay Packers, Wonnum recorded a strip sack on Aaron Rodgers which was recovered by teammate Eric Wilson late in the fourth quarter to secure a 28–22 Vikings' win.\nIn Week 10 against the Chicago Bears on Monday Night Football, Wonnum recorded a sack on Nick Foles during the 19–13 win.\nOn December 27, 2023, Wonnum was placed on the injured reserve list after suffering a season-ending torn quadriceps in a week 16 game against the Detroit Lions the previous Sunday.\n\nCAROLINA PANTHERS\nOn March 14, 2024, Wonnum signed a two-year deal with the Carolina Panthers. He was placed on the reserve/PUP list to start the season. He was activated on November 9.\nIn 2025, Wonnum played in 16 games with 15 starts, recording 42 tackles, three sacks, three passes defensed, and one interception.\n\nDETROIT LIONS\nOn March 17, 2026, Wonnum signed a one-year contract worth up to $6 million with the Detroit Lions.\nWonnum recorded his first Detroit sack against New York Jets quarterback Geno Smith. In Week 7 against the Green Bay Packers, Wonnum deflected a go-ahead field goal attempt from Trey Smack, allowing the Lions to eke out a 20-17 win and was named NFC Special Teams Player of the Week for his performance."},{"key":"personal","title":"Personal life","text":"Wonnum's younger brother, Dylan, was a starting offensive lineman at South Carolina."}],"wikidataId":"Q89806454","social":{}},"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4038849","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/W/WonnDJ00.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/dj-wonnum/44550","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/dj-wonnum/8857","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/D._J._Wonnum"},"insights":["Ranks 13th of 102 qualified edge defenders in sacks.","Ranks 16th of 107 qualified edge defenders in tackles for loss.","On the field for 52% of Detroit’s defensive snaps this season.","2026 cap number of $3.0M is the 19th-largest on the roster.","Contract expires after this season."]}